"use strict";(self.webpackChunknotes_by_sara=self.webpackChunknotes_by_sara||[]).push([["12161"],{56112(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"id":"FIN-028","slug":"financial-well-being","term":"Financial Well-Being","also_known_as":[],"difficulty":"Beginner","definition":"Financial well-being is a state in which you can meet your current financial commitments, feel secure about your financial future and have the freedom to make choices that let you enjoy life.","explanation":["Financial well-being is about more than income. Two people with the same salary can feel very differently about money depending on their debts, savings, spending habits and how much control they feel they have.","It usually has four parts. The first is control over day-to-day finances, meaning bills are paid on time and there is money left at the end of the month. The second is the ability to absorb a financial shock, such as an unexpected bill or loss of income. The third is being on track to meet future goals. The fourth is having enough freedom to make choices, such as taking a holiday, changing jobs or helping family, without serious worry.","Practical habits support financial well-being: keeping a budget, building an emergency fund, avoiding high-cost debt, saving regularly and having suitable insurance.","Employers, governments and researchers pay attention to financial well-being because money stress affects health, relationships and work performance. Improving it is often as much about habits and planning as about earning more."],"note":"","total":1725,"prev":{"slug":"financial-statement","term":"Financial Statement"},"next":{"slug":"finished-goods","term":"Finished Goods"}}')}}]);